 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Discursive differentiation between «da» and «weil»",
     "texto": [
      "1. **da (thematic or presupposed cause)**: typically used when the cause is already known to the interlocutors or is taken up from the previous context. For this stylistic reason, clauses with «da» very often head the sentence period (first position): **Da alle Fristen abgelaufen sind, müssen wir den Antrag ablehnen** (as all deadlines have expired, we must reject the application).",
      "2. **weil (new causal focus)**: introduces explanatory information that the listener does not know or that directly answers the question *Warum?*: **Wir lehnen den Antrag ab, weil wichtige Unterlagen fehlen**.",
      "3. Both connectors move the conjugated verb to the absolute end of the subordinate clause."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Causal connector",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Predominant informative function",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Most frequent sentence position",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "da",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Shared, evident or already mentioned cause («as / since»)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "At the start of the sentence period (Vorfeld)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "weil",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       },
       {
        "texto": "New informative cause or focused answer («because»)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Generally placed after the main clause",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
